From: OpenWrt MT6990 integration
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: terminate MT6990 QDMA FQ tail

The FG370 MT6990 SDK leaves txd2 of the final QDMA free-queue descriptor
zero.  The generic implementation links the final entry one descriptor past
the allocated ring.  Preserve the generic behaviour for existing SoCs and
replicate the SDK's terminated FQ chain for MT6990.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -1488,9 +1488,12 @@ static int mtk_init_fq_dma(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 
 			txd = eth->scratch_ring + TX_DESC_OFS(eth, j * MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH + i);
 			txd->txd1 = dma_addr + i * MTK_QDMA_PAGE_SIZE;
-			if (j * MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH + i < cnt)
+			if (j * MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH + i < cnt -
+			    (MTK_HAS_CAPS(soc->caps, MTK_SOC_MT6990) ? 1 : 0))
 				txd->txd2 = eth->phy_scratch_ring +
 					    TX_DESC_OFS(eth, j * MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH + i + 1);
+			else
+				txd->txd2 = 0;
 
 			txd->txd3 = TX_DMA_PLEN0(MTK_QDMA_PAGE_SIZE);
 			if (MTK_HAS_CAPS(soc->caps, MTK_36BIT_DMA))
